  "method": [
    "Compare the prior PR head 0ba4372b99 against batch-owned ordinary text documents, direct numeric JSON output, and direct base64 encoding. Baseline production is unchanged; both variants have identical expanded benchmark fixtures.",
    "Freeze binaries before measurement. Record hashes for numeric/media helpers, text collector and benchmark fixtures.",
    "Alternate baseline/candidate process order for eleven pairs per fixture, with one in-process warmup preceding each counted/timing sample. Bootstrap the paired median percentage changes with 10000 resamples and seed 9714. Negative changes mean faster.",
    "Unmeasured fixture construction uses the C allocator to avoid debugging overhead. Diagnostic runs use the C-backed allocation counter; timing runs use the production smp allocator. Setup, reference construction, and reporting are excluded; complete output validation is included.",
    "Ordinary text fixtures cover singleton (1000 docs) and batches 32,256,1024 (10000 docs). Mixed assets, missing documents, all-asset projections, sparse and relational collectors provide regression controls. JSON fixture documents counts renders; batch means numeric fields per render or input media bytes. Numeric renders use repeated maximum-u64 fields; media input cycles through all byte values.",
    "Assert equal complete output strings, matching checksums between variants, and zero counter live bytes after each measured run. Correctness and exhaustive allocation-failure tests retain the testing allocator.",
    "allocations means successful raw allocation calls. resize_calls/remap_calls count attempts including refusals. moving_remaps counts pointer changes and moved_bytes sums their requested new sizes. allocated_bytes is cumulative successful logical storage growth. Live/peak exclude allocator overhead, transient realloc overlap, and RSS.",
    "The slab retains the mandatory transaction-byte copy, uses checked exact-size allocation, and amortizes payload ownership for homogeneous ordinary public-document batches. Mixed/internal and relational batches retain existing per-value ownership and reservation behavior; inline values remain borrowed.",
    "Measurements are local experiments rather than production throughput guarantees or proof of universal zero overhead. They must not be pooled with earlier fixtures or ReleaseSafe exploratory measurements. The previously reported full-text repair integration failure remains unresolved; the broad integration suite was not rerun."
  ],
